        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ronway/{size}/1856_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-03-22T22:08:47.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>The card you are thinking of is Coolant Blast, which sadly only can hit non-hero targets.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>He can do&nbsp;a lot more than&nbsp;two&nbsp;infinite fire attacks to himself. If Imbued Fire is the card that is allowing him to deal fire, it is also allowing all heroes to do fire. Thus every hero could target Absolute Zero and chain as many infinite fire attacks as each hero can deal instances of damage. Most heroes have a one-shot that deals damage and a power that deals damage, so at least 2 damages from each hero (Visionary is the only one I can think of that wouldn't be able to help) so it is pretty much an auto win! Aside from the Dreamer, Chairman (if unflipped), and Miss Information (If unflipped), it'll probably single handily win any game where it turns up. Of Course after Christopher reads this there might be a change, maybe. As of right now it works as intended though!</p>",
        "post_number": 71,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:30:19.165Z",
