        "id": 55555,
        "name": "flamethrower49",
        "username": "flamethrower49",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/f/838e76/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2013-03-22T22:46:06.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Ameena\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ameena/48/1907_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Ameena:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Oh yeah, I wasn't suggesting that it \"shouldn't be allowed\" or anything like that, just that it's one extra interesting facet of the game and something to be careful of if such a situation comes up - you might have to somehow  protect  the Underbosses so that the environment didn't mess up your game. Nice if it takes out the Thugs, though ;).</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Yes, I imagine that if the Final Wasteland absolutely obliterates a certain number of the Chairman's dudes, his thought process will shift to stranding the heroes there while he gets back to his own time scot-free.&nbsp; Call it plan \"SCREW THIS.\"</p>",
