      {
        "id": 55556,
        "name": "Reckless",
        "username": "Reckless",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/reckless/{size}/2467_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-03-23T18:56:55.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Ameena\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ameena/48/1907_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Ameena:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>The thought has just occurred that UW coming out when fighting the Chairman has the potential to make the game unwinnable if three or more Underbosses are killed by the environment (while UW is out) before the Chairman flips…</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>A friend of mine brought that up in the playtesting forum.&nbsp; We gave it a shot to see how terrible it is.&nbsp; It's actually quite fun, because only the Chairman's Thugs were getting removed by the Environment.&nbsp; We whittled the Thugs down, had them eaten by UW, took out the Underbosses, and had an AMAZINGLY fun game against The Organization.&nbsp; Unforgiving Wasteland is a nightmare for them.</p>",
