      {
        "id": 55565,
        "name": "dypaca",
        "username": "dypaca",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/dypaca/{size}/2079_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-04-17T02:10:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Spiff\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/spiff/48/1865_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Spiff:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<blockquote>\nbut damage can't be less than 0\n</blockquote>\nhp couldn't be less than zero until recently too, so this may not be a fact to hang your hat on. ;) &nbsp;But at the moment, I agree with your assessment.\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>We've always had ways to reduce damage to a negative number.&nbsp; I'd say&nbsp;more accurately damage of less than one has no effect, but that's really quibbling over semantics.&nbsp; Also, to be clear, I would apply all damage modifiers to the negative base amount normally.&nbsp; So if Blade Battallion was at -1 HP, but two Obsidian fields were in play, I would have them deal 1 damage.</p>\n<p>The rule wording has always supported&nbsp;HP going negative, and the Advanced Matriarch's cohorts have always been able to survive this.&nbsp; All fixed point does is make it so cards that do things with their HP can get in on the fun.</p>\n<p>EDIT: although come to think of it,&nbsp;my Obsidian Field example makes no sense since obviously you can't have them and Fixed Point in play together, so lets say they attack Fixer with Bloody Knuckles out.</p>",
        "post_number": 82,
        "post_type": 1,
